.TH START-MU2EDAQ-CFOCONTROL.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-CFOControl t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start-mu2edaq-cfocontrol.sh \- control-room launcher for CFOControl.py
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start\-mu2edaq\-cfocontrol.sh
.RI [ CFOControl-option ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Standardised Mu2e control-room start script, run in a terminal by
.BR "crs-app start cfocontrol"
(entry
.B cfocontrol
in
.IR mu2edaq\-controlroom\-setup/config/apps.yaml ,
.BR "terminal: true" ).
It changes to its own directory, selects
.I ./venv/bin/python
if that file is executable and
.B python3
from
.B PATH
otherwise, and
.BR exec s
.PP
.RS
.B CFOControl.py \-\-port
.B $CRS_PORT_MACROMAKER
.RI [ CFOControl-option ...]
.RE
.PP
There is no daemon: the script ends when
.B CFOControl.py
exits.
Run with no arguments it lists the front-ends and exits.
.PP
Nothing in the package creates
.IR venv/ ,
and the superproject's
.I testing/common.sh
excludes this package from venv creation
.RB ( pkg_needs_venv ),
so in practice the system
.B python3
runs it and must have PyYAML installed.
.SH OPTIONS
All arguments are passed unchanged to
.BR CFOControl.py (1).
Because
.B \-\-port
is always passed first, a later
.B \-\-port
argument overrides it (argparse keeps the last value).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_MACROMAKER
Destination UDP port, default 5000.
It is always passed as
.BR \-\-port ,
so
.B connection.port
in
.I config.yaml
has no effect on this path.
The MacroMaker listens on whatever
.B OTS_MACROMAKER_UDP_PORT
is set to in its own environment; nothing in mu2edaq-main sets that variable,
so the two must be matched by hand.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./venv/bin/python
Interpreter used if present and executable.
.TP
.I CFOControl.py
.TP
.I config.yaml
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of
.BR CFOControl.py (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
cd ~/mu2edaq\-main/mu2edaq\-CFOControl
\&./start\-mu2edaq\-cfocontrol.sh \-\-host mu2e\-cfo\-01 \-\-fe CFO0
CRS_PORT_MACROMAKER=5001 ./start\-mu2edaq\-cfocontrol.sh \-\-host mu2e\-cfo\-01
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR CFOControl.py (1),
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-cfocontrol.sh (1),
.BR config.yaml (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
